<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      Compose draws the whole UI, so this only needs to set the window up and
      pick the colour of the launch flash before the first frame.

      The system bars are left to enableEdgeToEdge, which makes them
      transparent and lets the app bars paint behind them. Setting a colour here
      as well would fight it, and on Android 15+ the colour attributes are
      ignored regardless.

      This is the light value; values-night carries the dark one. The launch
      flash has to match the mode the app is about to compose in, or a light
      phone gets a black frame before the first Compose frame and a dark one
      gets a white flash — which is the same defect either way round, just
      pointed at whichever half of the users the single value was wrong for.
      Keep these two in step with `background` in the fallback schemes.
    -->
    <style name="Theme.DiveSlate" parent="android:Theme.Material.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">#F7FAFD</item>
    </style>
</resources>
